  "published": "2026-08-03T01:12:38.98Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v4.0.0-alpha.15: session revocation restored on the cookie path, plus role-tenant binding at registration -- read UPGRADE.md 28. BEHAVIOUR CHANGE: if your own Configure<CookieAuthenticationOptions> assigned options.Events wholesale after AddMyIdentity, Identity's SecurityStampValidator was silently dropped and a rotated security stamp stopped being enforced on every request that is not a Blazor circuit -- password reset, forced sign-out, account disable and tenant deactivation all stopped cutting the cookie. The library now detects that and chains the validator back on. If you dropped it deliberately, the sanctioned opt-out is options.EventsType, which discards options.Events entirely. If your own handler already calls SecurityStampValidator.ValidatePrincipalAsync itself, past the validation interval it now runs a second time after yours -- two round trips to the store and two principal reconstructions per such request, but the cookie is still re-issued only once. If your handler was enriching the principal with extra claims, move that to SecurityStampValidatorOptions.OnRefreshingPrincipal instead: past the validation interval the re-chained validator rebuilds the principal from the store, and claims added only inside OnValidatePrincipal do not survive that rebuild. BEHAVIOUR CHANGE: RegisterAsync now refuses a role owned by a different tenant with the new MyIdentityErrorCodes.RoleTenantMismatch; previously such a grant produced a ClaimTypes.Role the account's own tenant never granted, which any [Authorize(Roles=...)] in consumer code would honour. BEHAVIOUR CHANGE: an invalid MyIdentity:Authentication:DataProtection:KeyProtection now fails in the curated startup report instead of the raw binder exception, including a numeric value outside the enum. Added: MyIdentityMessageDescriber.RoleDoesNotBelongToTenant(). API may still change before stable.",
